mino_acids_and_evolution_of_the_triplet_code)\n  33. Order of amino acid recruitment into the genetic code resolved by last universal common ancestor\u2019s protein domains (https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2410311121)\n\n=== END DEEP RESEARCH FINDINGS ===\n\n\n\n=== END LITERATURE RESEARCH FINDINGS ===\n\nINSTRUCTIONS FOR LITERATURE-GUIDED SYNTHESIS:\n1. Prefer routes and conditions that are well supported experimentally in the research above.\n2. Weigh the critiques and contested points the research reports; do not adopt a route uncritically.\n3. You may depart from the described routes when the chemistry justifies it; explain why in \"reasoning\".\n4. Cite the supporting paper (author, year) in each reaction's \"reasoning\" field, or mark the reaction as speculative.\n", "raw_response": "{\n  \"target_molecule\": \"Arginine\",\n  \"overall_strategy\": \"This synthesis network integrates all literature-supported and credible speculative routes to arginine under prebiotic environments, as described in recent literature reviews. It features cyanosulfidic chemistry from HCN/acetylene/cyanamide (Patel et al., 2015), guanidinylation of ornithine (Longo et al., 2020), Strecker-like homologation, HCN-polymer hydrolysates, and plausible but unverified metabolic-like pathways. Each pathway traces a distinct chemical logic from C1/C2 precursors, through the C5 aminocarbon skeleton, to selective guanidinylation, and includes (where possible) both intermediates and the key bottleneck guanidinylation/hydrolysis events toward free arginine.\",\n  \"molecules\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_001\",\n      \"formula\": \"HCN\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"hydrogen cyanide\",\n      \"common_name\": null,\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/CHN/c1-2/h1H\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_002\",\n      \"formula\": \"NH3\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"azane\",\n      \"common_name\": \"ammonia\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/H3N/h1H3\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_003\",\n      \"formula\": \"C2H2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"ethyne\",\n      \"common_name\": \"acetylene\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C2H2/c1-2/h1-2H\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_004\",\n      \"formula\": \"CH2(CN)2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"malononitrile\",\n      \"common_name\": \"malononitrile\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C3H2N2/c4-2-1-3-5/h1-2H\",\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_005\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H3N\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"prop-2-enenitrile\",\n      \"common_name\": \"acrylonitrile\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C3H3N/c1-2-3-4/h2H,1H2\",\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_006\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H7N2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"3-aminopropanenitrile\",\n      \"common_name\": \"\u03b2-aminopropionitrile\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C3H6N2/c4-2-1-3-5/h1-2,4H2\",\n      \"role\": \"hub_intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_007\",\n      \"formula\": \"CH2N2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"cyanamide\",\n      \"common_name\": \"cyanamide\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/CH2N2/c2-1-3/h1H2\",\n      \"role\": \"hub_intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_008\",\n      \"formula\": \"C4H9N5\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"3-guanidinopropanenitrile\",\n      \"common_name\": \"guanidinylated \u03b2-aminopropionitrile\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C4H9N5/c5-2-1-3-9(6,7)4-8/h1-2,5H2,(H4,6,7,8)\",\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_009\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H7N\",\n      