null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": null\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Nucleophilic conjugate addition of NH3 to acrylonitrile produces \u03b2-aminopropionitrile.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Standard chemical logic; confirmed in the cyanosulfidic network (Patel et al., 2015).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_003\",\n      \"name\": \"Guanidinylation of \u03b2-aminopropionitrile by cyanamide\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_006\", \"mol_007\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_008\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-320K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"relatively inefficient\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"\u03b2-aminopropionitrile reacts with cyanamide, forming the N-guanidino nitrile.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Observed in Patel et al., 2015, but with incomplete conversion; efficiency limited in water.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_004\",\n      \"name\": \"Photoreduction of \u03b2-aminopropionitrile to \u03b2-aminopropionaldehyde\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_006\", \"mol_001\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_009\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"H2S (as HS\u2212) photoreductant\", \"UV light\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-320K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"Sulfidic conditions required\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"HS\u2212/UV photoreductive conversion of nitrile to aldehyde.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Key transformation in Kumar/Patel cyanosulfidic scheme (Patel et al., 2015).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_005\",\n      \"name\": \"Nucleophilic addition of cyanamide to \u03b2-aminopropionaldehyde\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_009\", \"mol_007\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_008\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-320K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"Proceeds efficiently (Patel et al.)\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Aldehyde reacts with cyanamide to give the guanidino adduct (eventually giving aminonitrile).\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Patel et al., 2015 found efficient conversion (77% yield); follows cyanosulfidic scheme closely.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_006\",\n      \"name\": \"Reductive homologation and Strecker reactions to arginine aminonitrile\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_008\", \"mol_002\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_013\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"H2S/HS\u2212 (photoreductant)\", \"UV light\", null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-330K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"H2S/HS\u2212 (photoreduction)\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"Carried out sequentially in cyanosulfidic flow\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Reductive successive additions and Strecker reactions extend the skeleton, forming the arginine \u03b1-aminonitrile, then hydrolyzed to arginine.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Step from guanidinylated adduct to arginine aminonitrile (designated '46' in Patel et al., 2015) tabulated but not directly demonstrated; hydrolysis to arginine is speculative.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_007\",\n      \"name\": \"Ornithine guanidinylation (cyanamide)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_010\", \"mol_007\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_013\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Biochemical\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-350K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"Slow, competing cyclization but plausible\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Free \u0