\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_010\", \"mol_014\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n      \"name\": \"Ornithine carbamoylation-citrulline-arginine\",\n      \"description\": \"Ornithine is carbamoylated by cyanate/carbamoyl phosphate to citrulline, then speculative transformation to arginine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_008\", \"rxn_009\", \"rxn_007\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_014\", \"mol_010\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n      \"name\": \"Skeletal construction from malononitrile (keto acid speculative pathway)\",\n      \"description\": \"Malononitrile and cyanamide build guanidinylated keto acid, which undergoes reductive amination to arginine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_011\", \"rxn_010\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_004\", \"mol_007\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"name\": \"Ammonium cyanide direct guanidinylating pathway\",\n      \"description\": \"Photolysis of HCN/ammonia gives cyanamide and guanidine, which interact in network with other intermediates toward arginine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_011\", \"rxn_012\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_006\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_007\", \"mol_012\", \"mol_013\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P9\",\n      \"name\": \"Reduction of guanidinylated intermediates (keto variant, speculative)\",\n      \"description\": \"Reductive amination of skeleton made from HCN-derived intermediates (e.g., malononitrile) with ammonia and cyanamide forms arginine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_011\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_010\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_004\", \"mol_007\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P10\",\n      \"name\": \"Sequential guanidinylation via carbamoylation (urea cycle analog, speculative)\",\n      \"description\": \"Follows hypothetical biological logic: ornithine formed from HCN/urea chemistry is carbamoylated to citrulline then converted to a