m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Arginine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: This synthesis network integrates all literature-supported and credible speculative routes to arginine under prebiotic environments, as described in recent literature reviews. It features cyanosulfidic chemistry from HCN/acetylene/cyanamide (Patel et al., 2015), guanidinylation of ornithine (Longo et al., 2020), Strecker-like homologation, HCN-polymer hydrolysates, and plausible but unverified metabolic-like pathways. Each pathway traces a distinct chemical logic from C1/C2 precursors, through the C5 aminocarbon skeleton, to selective guanidinylation, and includes (where possible) both intermediates and the key bottleneck guanidinylation/hydrolysis events toward free arginine.\n\nMOLECULES (17 nodes):\n  - mol_001: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_002: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_003: C2H2 (acetylene) [starting]\n  - mol_004: CH2(CN)2 (malononitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_005: C3H3N (acrylonitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_006: C3H7N2 (\u03b2-aminopropionitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_007: CH2N2 (cyanamide) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_008: C4H9N5 (guanidinylated \u03b2-aminopropionitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C3H7N (\u03b2-aminopropionaldehyde) [intermediate]\n  - mol_010: C4H11N3O2 (ornithine) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_011: CH4N2O (urea) [intermediate]\n  - mol_012: CH5N3 (guanidine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_013: C6H14N4O2 (arginine) [target]\n  - mol_014: C5H13N3O2 (citrulline) [intermediate]\n  - mol_015: C2O2NH (cyanate) [intermediate]\n  - mol_016: C5H9N3O4P (carbamoyl phosphate) [intermediate]\n  - mol_017: C5H11N3O2 (citrulline (ornithine adduct)) [intermediate]\n\nREACTIONS (12 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_001, mol_003 -> mol_005 (HCN homologation to acrylonitrile (Patel et al.)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_002: mol_005, mol_002 -> mol_006 (Acrylonitrile aminated to \u03b2-aminopropionitrile) [Surface]\n  - rxn_003: mol_006, mol_007 -> mol_008 (Guanidinylation of \u03b2-aminopropionitrile by cyanamide) [Surface]\n  - rxn_004: mol_006, mol_001 -> mol_009 (Photoreduction of \u03b2-aminopropionitrile to \u03b2-aminopropionaldehyde) [Surface]\n  - rxn_005: mol_009, mol_007 -> mol_008 (Nucleophilic addition of cyanamide to \u03b2-aminopropionaldehyde) [Surface]\n  - rxn_006: mol_008, mol_002 -> mol_013 (Reductive homologation and Strecker reactions to arginine aminonitrile) [Surface]\n  - rxn_007: mol_010, mol_007 -> mol_013 (Ornithine guanidinylation (cyanamide)) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_008: mol_001, mol_002, mol_011 -> mol_010, mol_014, mol_013 (HCN polymer hydrolysis to ornithine/citrulline/arginine (disputed)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_009: mol_010, mol_016 -> mol_014 (Ornithine carbamoylation to citrulline (cyanate or carbamoyl phosphate)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_010: mol_004, mol_007, mol_002 -> mol_013 (Metal/mineral-catalyzed reductive amination of 5-guanidino-2-oxopentanoate (speculative)) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_011: mol_001, mol_002 -> mol_007 (Formation of cyanamide from ammonium cyanide (photolysis)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_012: mol_001, mol_002 -> mol_012 (Formation of guanidine from ammonium cyanide (photolysis)) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Cyanosulfidic acrylonitrile homologation to arginine aminonitrile (4 steps)\n  - P2: Cyanosulfidic \u03b2-amin