ment\": 0.5,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.65,\n      \"feedback\": \"This pathway is the direct cyanosulfidic route supported by Patel et al. (2015) up to the guanidinylated \u03b2-aminopropionitrile or possibly the arginine aminonitrile. While the early steps are literature supported and use plausible surface conditions, the crucial guanidinylation (rxn_003) and final homologation/hydrolysis to arginine (rxn_006) lack mass balance (per balance check) and remain chemically unverified. Literature only demonstrates intermediates up to the aminonitrile. The atom balance errors (especially in rxn_003 and rxn_006) undermine the chemical feasibility, making target achievement speculative. Environmental consistency is good as these are well-matched to the studied cyanosulfidic system.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_003\", \"rxn_006\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Resolve atom balance in rxn_003 and rxn_006, identifying missing/omitted small molecules (e.g., NH3, HCN, H2O).\",\n        \"Explicitly clarify whether the pathway terminates at the aminonitrile or goes to free arginine, and if the latter, justify hydrolysis steps.\",\n        \"If possible, cite experimental or mechanistic evidence for the final steps, or clearly mark as speculative.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P2\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.95,\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.95,\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.60,\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.60,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.50\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.6,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.65,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.92,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.5,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.62,\n      \"feedback\": \"The \u03b2-aminopropionaldehyde branch replicates known cyanosulfidic intermediates (Patel et al.) but with steps (rxn_004, rxn_005, rxn_006) that are speculative, atom-unbalanced, and not literature-demonstrated for full arginine synthes