   \"Cite or design modern experiments confirming selectivity and yield.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_012\": 0.8,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.5,\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.6\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.55,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.62,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.9,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.5,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.58,\n      \"feedback\": \"This pathway involves guanidinylation via guanidine, with ancillary aminonitrile intermediates. The chemistry of guanidine generation from HCN/NH3 photolysis is supported (rxn_012), but the core guanidinylation (rxn_007, as above) is unbalanced and lacks experimental demonstration for free ornithine under prebiotic conditions. Pathway remains speculative, and environmental fit is adequate.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_007\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Clearly differentiate possible mechanisms (cyanamide vs. guanidine as guanidinylator) and their literature status.\",\n        \"Rectify atom balances and specify side products.\",\n        \"Restrict claims to intermediates unless in vitro demonstration is published.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.3\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.3,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.3,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.8,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.3,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.33,\n      \"feedback\": \"This pathway reflects the disputed HCN-polymer hydrolysate result (Matthews & Moser 1967), with rxn_008 massively atom-unbalanced and environmentally questionable (very harsh acid hydrolysis at high temperature). Modern re-analyses do not confirm the arginine claim. No verifiable mechanism from HCN to arginine via hydrolysate is specified. Should be treated as historically interesting but not plausible.\",\n      \"app