otic UV.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_014\",\n      \"name\": \"Reductive homologation of cyanamide to guanidine\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_011\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_012\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"UV light\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"310\u2013330K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": \"true\",\n        \"other\": \"UV irradiation\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Condensation and reduction of cyanamide yields guanidine.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Prebiotic photoreduction routes (Lohrmann 1972); guanidine found in HCN photolysates.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_015\",\n      \"name\": \"Hypothetical Fe/Ni-catalyzed reductive amination to ornithine skeleton\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_012\", \"mol_001\", \"mol_002\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_010\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"FeS/Fe(OH)2 mineral surfaces\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"370\u2013420K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"FeS, Fe(OH)2\",\n        \"aqueous\": \"true\",\n        \"other\": \"Anoxic, mineral surface\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Reductive amination of suitable C5 keto acid or intermediate by guanidine and ammonia yields ornithine.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"No direct experimental data for arginine/ornithine, but robust precedent for other amino acids in vent chemistry (Mayer & Moran 2022; Barge et al. 2019). Treated as speculative for this skeleton.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pathways\": [\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n      \"name\": \"Cyanosulfidic Prebiotic (Patel et al. \u2018direct\u2019 route)\",\n      \"description\": \"Feedstock (HCN, acetylene, ammonia) undergoes Cu-catalyzed homologation, then Michael addition and photoredox steps leading to the arginine \u03b1-aminonitrile (intermediate 46). Final hydrolysis to arginine is plausible but u